// What a backup keeps, radio by radio, from the record the flasher's backup step reads.
import BackupGaps from '../components/BackupGaps.astro';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="What a backup keeps"
  description="For each radio, whether the flasher's backup holds everything, and what it cannot save yet."
  current="backups"
>
  <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-3xl prose-a:text-primary">
    <p>
      Before it flashes, the flasher offers to back the radio up: a copy of what is on it, to go back to if you need
      to. For most radios that copy is not whole yet. This page says, radio by radio, what it leaves out and what that
      would cost you, so you can decide before you flash. It is written from the same record the flasher's backup step
      reads.
    </p>
    <BackupGaps />
    <p>
      The memory map behind this page, with sizes, the ranges read and how each read was checked, is in the flasher's{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/turnrye/openrtx-web-flasher/blob/main/docs/backup-coverage.md"
        >backup coverage notes</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
